# Collection views

The notebook in [[field-notes]] has three useful keyed views.

| Type | Key contract | Key projection |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Map<String, Int>` | Each species has one count | `Set<String>` |
| `OrderedMap<String, Int>` | Keys retain construction positions | `Seq<String>` |
| `SortedMap<String, Int>` | Key positions follow String order | `Seq<String>` |

A map has its own lookup contract. It is not a collection of entries.
Its keys can be projected into a collection and queried there.

```hql#eval
route = OrderedMap(
    ["european-robin", "barn-owl", "common-raven"],
    [1, 2, 1]
)
alphabet = SortedMap(
    ["european-robin", "barn-owl", "common-raven"],
    [1, 2, 1]
)

{
    route: route.keys,
    alphabet: alphabet.keys,
    owl_observations: get(alphabet, "barn-owl"),
}
```

The ordered route begins at [[european-robin]]. The sorted keys begin at
[[barn-owl]], followed by [[common-raven]] and the robin. Changing a map's static
view to `Map<String, Int>` exposes set semantics for its keys while retaining
the same associations.

A repeated key is rejected during construction. Use a list for repeated
observations and a map for the single count associated with each species.
